' The extension file of Vibe Commander: what Enter does with a file
' by its extension. A line such as
'
'   txt: edit !.!
'
' has Enter on a .TXT file run that command; ? stands for any
' character of the extension and * for any rest, ! for the file's
' name and !.! for its name and extension.
'
' A web page cannot run commands, so this file has no entry: Enter on
' a file that no entry names opens it in a new tab of the browser.
' Take the apostrophe off the line below to see what an entry does.
'
'bat: type !.!
